WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Tonight's
"Second Chance Theatre"

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:04.471
is a sketch that you guys worked
on together called "Unicorn.

00:00:04.471 --> 00:00:08.141 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's right.
Yeah, this was from the --

00:00:08.141 --> 00:00:13.413
one of the last episodes of my
first year writing for "SNL.

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:14.948 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
So 2010.

00:00:14.948 --> 00:00:22.188 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it went to dress with
an actress named Betty White

00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:22.622 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:25.792
From the very beginning, thi
sketch was an uphill battle.

00:00:25.792 --> 00:00:27.060 line:92%
Betty was not fully on board

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:30.130 align:start size:94% position:6%
Can you talk a little bit
about the why?

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:35.201 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. So, I got just
kind of blindsided by this

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:36.536 align:start size:94% position:6%
I got called
into her dressing room.

00:00:36.536 --> 00:00:40.507 align:start size:94% position:6%
It had gone well on Wednesday,
and I assumed she liked

00:00:40.507 --> 00:00:43.543 align:start size:94% position:6%
that it was getting laughs
and people were nice about it.

00:00:43.543 --> 00:00:46.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I got called
into her dressing room

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:47.447 size:81% position:41% line:92%
on Friday or Saturday.

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:52.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
And her manager,
who's much older than her...

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:53.787 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.787 --> 00:00:58.324 align:start size:94% position:6%
...started to lay into me
and slapping the coffee tabl

00:00:58.324 --> 00:01:00.860 line:92%
saying, "We said no animals!

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:03.463 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-And I was just flabbergasted.

00:01:03.463 --> 00:01:07.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
We didn't have an actual horse
playing the unicorn even.

00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:11.071 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was always
a very fake stuffed animal

00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:12.839 line:92%
So I was confused by that.

00:01:12.839 --> 00:01:15.875 line:92%
And then I tried to talk to them

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:19.279 size:81% position:41%
about how the unicorns
aren't actual animals.

00:01:19.279 --> 00:01:24.150 align:start size:94% position:6%
And how there is kind of a fun
in that Betty White is

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:29.589
the most unlikely of people to
be this cold unicorn euthanizer.

00:01:29.589 --> 00:01:30.590 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:33.426 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And we just kind of lost --
and then our concession,

00:01:33.426 --> 00:01:37.363
we realized this week when w
looked back at the final dress

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:40.733 align:start size:94% position:6%
script was we put
a paragraph at the end

00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:43.736 align:start size:94% position:6%
where Betty says,
"No unicorns were hurt."

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:44.404 size:75% position:38% line:92%
And it's not a joke.

00:01:44.404 --> 00:01:48.942 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's for other people out ther
who are maybe worried.

00:01:48.942 --> 00:01:52.545 align:start size:94% position:6%
A bizarre jokeless
moment in "SNL."

00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:53.213 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yep.

00:01:53.213 --> 00:01:56.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And now there was, you know
I think all three of us

00:01:56.416 --> 00:02:00.520 align:start size:94% position:6%
would agree "SNL" has
the best staff in the world.

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:02.422 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yep.
-The best props, best wardrobe

00:02:02.422 --> 00:02:04.390 align:start size:94% position:6%
best hair and makeup,
and when you first brought

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:08.461
this sketch to them, it wasn't
necessarily going to just be

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:09.629 size:78% position:39% line:92%
fake unicorns, right?

00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:15.568
-Yeah, they offered to get
a horse and put a horn on it

00:02:15.568 --> 00:02:17.437 line:92%
-Which, now that, that to me

00:02:17.437 --> 00:02:21.841 align:start size:94% position:6%
seems like some animal cruelty
by default.

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:22.742 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-That's a good point.

00:02:22.742 --> 00:02:25.211 align:start size:94% position:6%
We probably should've let them
know, like, Betty know

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:28.615
and her manager that, hey, w
could have gone this route

00:02:28.615 --> 00:02:30.783 line:92%
and we didn't because of you

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:34.020
The only other option was
I think Lorne's daughter

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:35.221 line:92%
at that time had a real unicorn,

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:36.823 size:84% position:42%
which I know we're not
supposed to talk about.

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:38.224 line:92%
-Right, I know, very much so

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:41.060
I think Lorne showed us pictures
and said --

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:42.929 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:42.929 --> 00:02:45.598
Now, it should be noted
because I do want to take

00:02:45.598 --> 00:02:48.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
some of this onus off
Betty White.

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:50.770 line:92%
You did try it one other time.

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:54.674 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, in my third season,
we did it with Ferrell.

00:02:54.674 --> 00:02:56.409 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's more the version
that we're doing for

00:02:56.409 --> 00:02:58.511 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Second Chance Theatre"
where it's a little bit more

00:02:58.511 --> 00:03:04.083
about the back-and-forth between
what was Jason and Ferrell

00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:09.522
-Will Ferrell, one of the
all-time greatest sketch actors.

00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:10.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-Yeah.

00:03:10.523 --> 00:03:13.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, not that Colin Farrel
wouldn't have crushed it,

00:03:13.793 --> 00:03:17.564 align:start size:94% position:6%
totally capable.
Um, but, yeah.

00:03:17.564 --> 00:03:19.632 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Yeah, giving it his all.

00:03:19.632 --> 00:03:22.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And Will Ferrell liked it
and tried really hard.

00:03:22.969 --> 00:03:29.676
In my memories, it went medium
then, or it maxes out at medium.

00:03:29.676 --> 00:03:31.244 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:31.244 --> 00:03:34.347
-And now the other thing that'
very -- so now we're admitting

00:03:34.347 --> 00:03:37.750
right now we're about to sho
people a sketch that bombed with

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:41.521 align:start size:94% position:6%
Betty White and only did mediu
with Will Ferrell.

00:03:41.521 --> 00:03:44.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is this the worst -- was
Betty White "Unicorn" the wors

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:48.962 align:start size:94% position:6%
either of you ever bombed
at dress?

00:03:48.962 --> 00:03:51.864 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Ooh.
-I have one worse.

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:53.032 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And it was --

00:03:53.032 --> 00:03:57.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
Mulaney and I wrote one wher
we'd read a true story

00:03:57.937 --> 00:04:00.073 size:75% position:38% line:92%
that Stephen Hawking

00:04:00.073 --> 00:04:03.610 align:start size:94% position:6%
was seen going to a strip club
in England.

00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:04.244 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:04:04.244 --> 00:04:08.881
-And that the guy in the article
was interviewed as saying,

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:11.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Yeah, every time he comes in,
I always say,

00:04:11.384 --> 00:04:13.319 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Stephen, do you want to tal
about planets

00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:14.487 align:start size:94% position:6%
or do you want to
just look at the ladies?'"

00:04:14.487 --> 00:04:17.724 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Stephen always says,
"Just the ladies this time."

00:04:17.724 --> 00:04:20.660 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so Mulaney and I wrote
a sketch about

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:22.996 line:92%
what an idiot that guy would be.

00:04:22.996 --> 00:04:26.032
But as soon as Fred came out
in a wheelchair and was, like,

00:04:26.032 --> 00:04:29.669 align:start size:94% position:6%
talking in an electronic voice
the audience --

00:04:29.669 --> 00:04:32.071 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I think
some crew guys walked out.

00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:33.273 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yep.

00:04:33.273 --> 00:04:37.343
-And it should be noted this was
not some ad homonym attack

00:04:37.343 --> 00:04:39.746 align:start size:94% position:6%
This was ripped
from the headlines.

00:04:39.746 --> 00:04:41.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yep.
-Yes.

00:04:41.914 --> 00:04:44.417 size:81% position:41%
-I should say it was
ripped from a headline

00:04:44.417 --> 00:04:45.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
that not a lot of people
had seen.

00:04:45.418 --> 00:04:48.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it definitely felt like
you had made it up.

00:04:48.421 --> 00:04:49.389 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:49.389 --> 00:04:52.492
-Which just seems like it'
such a random weird thing

00:04:52.492 --> 00:04:53.192 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
to say about him.

00:04:53.192 --> 00:04:54.227 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There's a couple things
we should note

00:04:54.227 --> 00:04:56.863
and then we're going to come
back and watch this thing.

00:04:56.863 --> 00:04:59.365 align:start size:94% position:6%
One, obviously, it was meant t
be a live sketch.

00:04:59.365 --> 00:05:01.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
We shot it
in three different locations

00:05:01.868 --> 00:05:07.040 align:start size:94% position:6%
Two, the children were alway
played by cast members.

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:10.476 align:start size:94% position:6%
So you had people like
Nasim Pedrad and Abby Elliot

00:05:10.476 --> 00:05:13.246 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Vanessa Bayer
all playing children.

00:05:13.246 --> 00:05:17.083 align:start size:94% position:6%
We did -- Sudeikis and I -
we used our kids.

00:05:17.083 --> 00:05:20.386 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think it adds
to the verisimilitude

00:05:20.386 --> 00:05:23.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
of a mythological beast sketch
called "Unicorn."

00:05:23.189 --> 00:05:25.692 size:78% position:39%
So we're going to all
watch it together,

00:05:25.692 --> 00:05:27.660 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then we're going to come
back and talk about it.

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:31.197
Everybody stick around
for the first performance

00:05:31.197 --> 00:05:33.700 line:92%
on television of "Unicorn.

